Z||000014||Fierowrecker||09-03-2001||05:59 AM||||Hey Ken!<BR>Have you done anything to your suspention at all???<BR>I added the rear sway bar to mine by using a front bar off another Fiero, and that added a lot of stability in the corners...<BR>I just finished rebuilding my front end, added poly upper and lower bushings, new ball joints upper and lower, and new sensa-track shocks, that helped too!<BR>I did the front end with $250 in parts, I didn't shop around, just went to NAPA, cept the poly, got that from the Fiero store...<BR>Can't wait to do the rear suspention!<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Tryxalon||09-03-2001||09:48 AM||||I don't know but if the stock 85 handles better than your's MooCow, I'd think that<BR> A) something is worn or<BR> B) inproperly adjusted <BR>on your car. <P> I'd put it in the air and give the entire suspension a good "shake rattle and roll" to see if something is "off". <P>I sounds like shocks to me as well.  <P>||||reg||1
